ook will not  provide you with more shares of stock  just because the share price Falls  instead a set number of shares are  determined when you get hired usually  these stock plans are set up to last  four years from the day you get hired so  if you get hired as a Facebook director  you wouldn't be offered 881 000 per year  rather you'd be offered 3.5 million  dollars for the next four years at  antichran share prices from there you'll  get access to a portion of this talk  every year this might not sound like a  big difference but it definitely can be  for example imagine that you were hired  at Facebook in September of 2021 since  then Facebook stock has plummeted it 70  which would mean that your 881 000 worth  of stock is only worth 264 000 by the  time you get it now of course that still  adds up to a total compensation of seven  hundred thousand dollars but that's  almost half of a 1.3 million despite the  fact that you're doing the same job now  imagine that this same scenario took  place in Netflix Netflix stock has also  crashed as much as 75 since their Peak  last year but if you're a Netflix  director earning 1.3 million dollars  last year you'd still be earning the  full 1.3 million as long as you didn't  get laid off of course a similar  argument could be made for the health  insurance credit as well usually a  substantial number of employees don't  even use the company provided health  insurance because they're covered by the  your spouse's company or their parents  company or whatever the case may be this  is awesome for companies given that they  can boast about having great insurance  plans while not even having to pay for a  bunch of their employees on the flip  side this sucks for employees given that  health insurance is technically a part  of the total compensation but they're  not actually receiving it Netflix's  health insurance credit however would  ensure that employees aren't fully left  out while employees that won't be able  to leverage 