e able to buy  nearly as much stock as Facebook or  Google offered you due to the second  shortfall of cash salaries which is high  taxes when you're earning seven figures  in cash you can bet that the government  is going to tax the hell out of you if  you're in California it's probably going  to be over 50 percent meanwhile if you  had a lot of stock compensation you'd  still be paying a massive tax tax bill  but maybe you could reduce the  percentage to something closer to forty  percent and when we're talking about  seven figure salaries that's an extra  six figures that you get to keep  something else to note is that the  unlimited vacation time is also not as  good as it may seem at first glance you  see it employees generally feel bad when  you take time off in an unlimited PTO  environment and on average they actually  end up taking too fewer days off per  year so Netflix ends up coming off as  the nice employer that offers unlimited  time off even though that doesn't  actually translate to more time being  taken off also most companies have a  policy of paying out accrued PTO when  you leave the company under good terms  for companies with unlimited PTO though  there is no accrued PTO so they can  avoid paying that so while such policies  do have their perks they're by no means  perfect either  foreign  Netflix has taken an approached a  compensation that's extremely uncommon  not only do they pay fat Tech salaries  but they paid all in cash this is  largely due to their philosophy and  extraordinary profitability while there  are advantages and the disadvantages to  this compensation structure I very much  think that it's a step in the right  direction giving employees more control  of how they get paid is never a bad  thing now of course with no structured  health insurance plans or retirement  plans there's gonna be some Bozo who  spent all the cash and has no money left  when they have a health emergency or are  approaching retirement but for the rest  